      "documentConcept": "Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb",
      "text": "Living well with PD includes individualized decisions about driving and employment, practical preparation for travel, and adapting personally important daily activities. The Parkinson\u2019s Foundation recommends assessing driving in light of symptoms and medication effects, considering workplace adaptations, and planning medication access and rest when traveling. Occupational therapy offers personalized task and routine strategies. A randomized trial supports improvement in self-perceived daily activity performance, while driving research cautions against equating simulator or test impairment with proven increases in real-world crashes. Patient stories illustrate practical barriers but do not establish universal solutions.",
